source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A `!` directly before a word rune does not close an image, so the row is three cells.
-- input.jira --
||h1||h2||
|!a.png|b!x|c|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h1</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h2</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>!a.png</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>b!x</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>c</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h1||h2||
|!a.png|b!x|c|
:::
